{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794746360,"nonce":"x3aNF5mWkjFU5jQK5VqLtoBtqtU=","message":"A richer IR: the facts the TAST can put on AIR, mapped to what the passes refuse to do today. Read from air/src/v2/passes/{licm,gvn,sroa,escape}.rs.\n\nWhat the passes say they cannot do:\n- licm and gvn move or reuse a `ReadMem` load only if nothing in the loop writes an aliasing class and nothing clobbers all memory. Every call is `ClobberAll`, so one call pins every invariant load beside it. A hoisted load must also sit in a block that dominates every exit, because speculating it could fault.\n- sroa: \"in HL `new C(...)` hands the fresh object straight to the constructor, so every allocation escapes into a call until that constructor has been inlined\". Escape analysis has the same rule for any call argument, and escape.rs needs \"every field the loop reads is written first\", which it gets only after inlining.\n\nFacts to supply, in the order they unlock the most (each lands with the pass that uses it and is measured alone):\n1. Call effect summaries. The lowering knows the exact callee (devirtualized, specialized), so it can give each call the storage classes it reads and writes, whether it allocates or throws, and per parameter whether the argument escapes, is stored, or is only field-read. Replaces ClobberAll. Unlocks licm, gvn, cellfwd and the escape rule for arguments.\n2. Constructor shape. A `new C(a, b)` whose constructor only initializes its own fields (no virtual call, `this` does not escape) lowers as one aggregate construction instead of New plus a call. sroa and escape then see the allocation without inlining, and \"fields written first\" holds by construction. The mandelbrot shape.\n3. Immutability. `final` fields are already in the file; add fields written only in constructors, found by a whole-program scan (the closed world makes it exact). Loads of them are loop-invariant across calls and never clobbered. Closure environments: a captured local that is not wrapped by CPWrapRef is never reassigned, so its environment field is immutable.\n4. Non-null. Results of `new`, `this`, string literals, value types, final fields assigned non-null in the constructor. Lets licm speculate a load that could not fault, and lets nullcheck drop checks.\n5. Exact receivers and type-based aliasing. Exact class from `new`, from final classes, and from the closed world; a store to `Foo.x` cannot alias a load of `Bar.y`; distinct instantiations after layout specialization are distinct classes, which is a finer alias split than the bytecode had.\n6. Ranges that follow from types and constructs: UInt, Bool, enum index in [0, n) (so an exhaustive switch needs no default and no bounds check), array length \u003e= 0, `x \u0026 mask`, `x % n`, 8- and 16-bit loads.\n7. Loop and bounds facts: a while loop from `for (i in 0...n)` is recognizable in the file (ForRemap has run), with the array and bound not reassigned in the body, so the bounds check is provably redundant; `@:ash.unchecked` on an expression says so directly.\n8. No-throw and no-safepoint regions (no throw node, only calls to no-throw callees; no allocation), for try regions and for loop passes that need no GC point.\n\nAIR slots this needs, to add as each pass takes them: a call-summary id on Call/CallMethod, an immutable flag on FieldGet, a non-null and range annotation on values, and an aggregate-construction form of New. User hints (`@:ash.noThrow`, `@:ash.pure`, `@:ash.unchecked`) feed the same slots where the analysis cannot prove the fact.","files":null}]}